    "c2511f7d-3681-4606-a9d6-d3f305fbf1f8": {
      "id": "c2511f7d-3681-4606-a9d6-d3f305fbf1f8",
      "message": {
        "id": "c2511f7d-3681-4606-a9d6-d3f305fbf1f8",
        "author": {
          "role": "assistant",
          "name": null,
          "metadata": {}
        },
        "create_time": 1773428867.530952,
        "update_time": null,
        "content": {
          "content_type": "text",
          "parts": [
            "In **entity[\"country\",\"Canada\"]**, you **do NOT need to show or deposit money to create a political party**. However, there are **administrative requirements** with the federal election authority, **entity[\"organization\",\"Elections Canada\"]**. 🇨🇦\n\n### Requirements to Register a Federal Political Party\nTo register a party in Canada you must:\n\n1. **Have at least 250 members**\n   - They must be **eligible voters in Canada**.\n   - They must sign declarations supporting the party.\n\n2. **Provide party leadership information**\n   - Party **leader**\n   - **Chief agent** (handles finances)\n   - **Auditor** (must be a licensed accountant)\n\n3. **Submit the party name and logo**\n   - It cannot be confusingly similar to existing parties.\n\n4. **Provide party constitution and purpose**\n   - Outline the **political goals** and structure.\n\n5. **Candidate requirement**\n   - The party must **endorse at least one candidate in a federal election** to maintain registration.\n\n### Money Rules (Important)\nYou **do not need to show money**, but:\n\n- The party must open a **bank account**.\n- All **donations and spending must follow Canadian election finance laws**.\n- Financial reports must be filed with **entity[\"organization\",\"Elections Canada\"]**.\n\n### Donations Limits (Example)\nIndividuals can donate a limited amount each year (about **$1,700+**, adjusted yearly).  \nCorporations and unions **cannot donate federally**.\n\n### Benefits of Being Registered\nA registered party can:\n\n- Issue **tax receipts for donations**.\n- Have the **party name on ballots**.\n- Receive some **reimbursements for election expenses**.\n\n### Interesting Fact\nCanada has **many small registered parties**, including:\n\n- entity[\"political_party\",\"Green Party of Canada\"]  \n- entity[\"political_party\",\"People's Party of Canada\"]  \n- entity[\"political_party\",\"Marijuana Party of Canada\"]  \n\nSome started with **very small groups of supporters**.\n\n✅ **Summary:**  \nYou **don’t need to show money**, but you must show **members, leadership, and financial compliance**.\n\n---\n\nIf you want, I can also explain:\n\n- **How to start a political party step-by-step in Canada (practical guide)**  \n- **How much money it realistically takes to run one candidate**  \n- **How small parties grow into national parties**."
          ]
        },
