    "73a5791e-0e5e-4eee-9ba4-898e550b5e52": {
      "id": "73a5791e-0e5e-4eee-9ba4-898e550b5e52",
      "message": {
        "id": "73a5791e-0e5e-4eee-9ba4-898e550b5e52",
        "author": {
          "role": "assistant",
          "name": null,
          "metadata": {}
        },
        "create_time": 1773428867.484078,
        "update_time": null,
        "content": {
          "content_type": "text",
          "parts": [
            "In **entity[\"country\",\"Canada\"]**, you **do not need to show a large amount of money** to create a federal political party, but you **must meet certain legal requirements** set by **entity[\"organization\",\"Elections Canada\"]**.\n\n### Main Requirements to Register a Political Party\n\n1. **Party Leader**\n   - You must declare an official leader.\n\n2. **250 Members**\n   - At least **250 eligible voters in Canada** must sign a declaration supporting the party.\n\n3. **Party Officers**\n   - At least **three officers** (besides the leader).\n\n4. **Chief Agent**\n   - Someone responsible for finances.\n\n5. **Auditor**\n   - A licensed auditor must be appointed.\n\n6. **Party Name**\n   - The name must not be confusingly similar to an existing party.\n\n7. **Application Forms**\n   - Submit official forms to **entity[\"organization\",\"Elections Canada\"]**.\n\n### Do You Need to Show Money?\nNo minimum bank balance is required to register.  \nHowever, once registered:\n\n- You must **report all donations and expenses**.\n- If you raise or spend money, **financial statements must be filed yearly**.\n- Campaign expenses must follow limits during elections.\n\n### Optional but Practical\nMost parties still open:\n- a **party bank account**\n- a **donation system**\n\nbecause campaigning requires funding.\n\n### Example of Existing Federal Parties\nSome registered parties include:\n- entity[\"organization\",\"Liberal Party of Canada\"]  \n- entity[\"organization\",\"Conservative Party of Canada\"]  \n- entity[\"organization\",\"New Democratic Party\"]  \n- entity[\"organization\",\"Green Party of Canada\"]  \n\n---\n\n✅ **In short:**  \nYou **don’t have to prove you have money**, but you **must show organizational support (250 members) and follow financial reporting rules**.\n\n---\n\nIf you want, I can also explain:\n- **How someone could start a party in Canada step-by-step**\n- **How much it realistically costs to run one**\n- **How small parties get funding from the government**."
          ]
        },
